{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Seven days you shall eat unleavened bread.</b> He commanded that the Festival of Unleavened Bread be seven days, and He called the first day and the seventh day a holy convocation, for the first is the day of redemption and the seventh is the conclusion of redemption. Now you already know that these seven days correspond to the six directions (sides) together with HaShem, all of them rejoicing in His joy. And this is the reason we were charged regarding the joy of the Festival (yom tov), which Scripture calls חדות ה׳ — 'the joy of HaShem' — as it is written concerning the Festival (Nehemiah 8:10): ״כי חדות ה' היא מעוזכם״, and this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:06.523127356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}